course: dictionary
lesson: 7923
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. The dictionary gives reaction several meanings. «Her reaction to the news was a big smile» means what she did or felt because of the news.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Never share food with someone who has an allergy; even a tiny amount can cause a dangerous reaction» is about the body responding badly, because of the allergy and the danger. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Science uses reaction in a special way. When vinegar and bicarbonate of soda fizz, that is a chemical reaction: the substances change into new ones. Quick reaction is different again, meaning how fast you respond, as when you catch a ball.
fact: Reaction can mean what someone says, does or feels because of something that has happened.
fact: A chemical reaction is when substances change into new substances, such as vinegar and bicarbonate of soda fizzing.
fact: Signs of a chemical reaction include fizzing, a colour change, heat or light, or a new solid forming.
fact: An allergic reaction is when the body responds badly to something, such as nuts or a bee sting.
fact: «Reaction time» means how quickly you respond to something.
exercise: «Vinegar and bicarbonate of soda fizz together: that is a chemical reaction.» What has happened in this sentence? | The vinegar has been poured away | The liquid has been frozen solid | The bottle has been shaken hard | *The substances have changed into new substances
exercise: «Her quick reaction helped her catch the ball.» What does quick reaction mean here? | A loud shout from the crowd | *How fast she responded | A red rash on her arm | A push back in the opposite direction
exercise: «A bee sting gave him an allergic reaction, with a swollen face.» What does this tell you? | His face was painted for a party | He was pleased with the bee | *His body responded badly to the sting | He was stung by two bees by mistake
test: «No atom is lost in a reaction; the atoms are only rearranged.» Which word tells you this sentence is about science? | *atoms | soft | quickly | happy
test: «The doctor writes the reaction in the patient's record.» What does reaction probably mean here? | A big cheer at a football match | A new experiment with colourful liquids in a lab | A fast game of tag in the playground | *How the patient's body responded to a medicine
exam: If someone has a swollen face and trouble breathing after a sting, what should you do? | Give them a long drink of cold water | Wait and see if it goes away by itself | *Call for help at once | Tell them it is only a chemical reaction
